* `CompleteLattice` (Theorem 3.6): the pretorsion theories of `mod Λ`, ordered
  by `(T, F) ≤ (T', F')` iff `T ⊆ T'` and `F ⊇ F'`, form a complete lattice,
  with the meet and join of a nonempty family given by (3.2) and (3.3) and with
  `(0, mod Λ)` and `(mod Λ, 0)` as least and greatest elements.
* `TheoremBPretorsion` and `TheoremBImageClosed` (Theorem B = Theorems 7.5 and
  8.5 at `x = 1`): for the linearly oriented quiver `1 → 2 → ⋯ → n`, the
  pretorsion theories counted by the number of indecomposables in `T ∩ F`, and
