Conventions follow the manuscript. `k` is an arbitrary field and `Λ` a
finite-dimensional `k`-algebra. Modules are finite-dimensional right modules,
realized as finitely generated modules over `Λᵐᵒᵖ`. A subcategory is a
property of objects closed under isomorphisms, finite direct sums and direct
